cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this technical note, please cite it as below."
title: "Certified Weil Positivity at L = 4/5: Two-Sided Bounds, Parity Separation, and Cutoff Diagnostics"
abstract: >-
  A computer-assisted two-sided bound on the spectral infimum of the window Weil
  form at L = 4/5 in one fixed normalization: 1.41e-17 <= lambda_Q(4/5) <=
  1.9014e-17. The lower bound comes from a frequency-cutoff comparison at T = 400
  reduced to a 440-dimensional Legendre block, verified by a preconditioned
  congruence in Arb ball arithmetic with a super-exponentially small complement
  estimate and a Schur-type coupling bound, in both parity sectors. The upper
  bound is the Rayleigh quotient of the original form at one explicit even
  rational test function, evaluated in the time domain. A separate certificate
  gives lambda_Q,odd >= 2.3e-17, which exceeds the upper bound and so identifies
  the even infimum as the one that determines lambda_Q. Diagnostics at cutoffs
  T in {200, 400, 800} bound the gain available from a larger cutoff. This is a
  single-window computation; it establishes no arithmetic estimate, no statement
  about the location of any zeta zero, and nothing about the Riemann hypothesis.
  Technical note, not peer-reviewed.
